====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# Someone or something who [[bark#Etymology_2|bark]]s.
#: {{syn|en|latrant|latrator|q1=obsolete}}
#: {{ux|en|My neighbor's dog is a constant '''barker''' that keeps me awake at night.}}
#* {{RQ:Lindsay Age of Consent|year=1962|page=42|passage=Edmund was '''barker''' on sight, like foolish stay-at-home dogs.}}
# A person employed to [[solicit]] [[customer]]s by calling out to passersby, e.g. at a [[carnival]].
#: {{syn|en|tout|spruiker|q2=Australia}}
#: {{hyponyms|en|doorsman}}
#: {{ux|en|Bob had amassed a considerable stockpile of double entendres from his days working as a '''barker''' for a strip joint.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=The Adventures of a Country Boy at a Country Fair|author=James Otis|year=1893|url=https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/37647/pg37647-images.html|passage={{...|Then they stopped at the "envelope game," where were spread on a stand a large collection of cheap, gaudy goods, each bearing a printed number, every one supposed to correspond with those contained in a box of envelopes, and }} this fakir was doing a big business, as was shown by the fact that he could afford to hire a '''barker''', who cried continually at the full strength of his lungs: "Come up now, and try your luck! {{...}}"}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2013-06-07|author=David Simpson|volume=188|issue=26|page=36|magazine={{w|The Guardian Weekly}}|title=Fantasy of navigation|url=http://www.guardian.co.uk/books/2013/may/18/falling-upwards-richard-holmes-review|passage=For every dedicated scientist patiently recording atmospheric pressure and wind speed while shivering at high altitudes, there is a carnival '''barker''' with a bevy of pretty girls willing to dangle from a basket or parachute down to earth.}}
# A [[shelf-talker]].
# {{lb|en|video games}} A video game mode where the action is demonstrated to entice someone to play the game.
#: {{ux|en|The '''barker''' looks action-packed, but actually playing the game is rather dull}}
# {{lb|en|slang|dated}} A [[pistol]].
#: {{synonyms|en|barking iron}}
#* {{RQ:Dickens Oliver Twist}}
#*: Barney, opening a cupboard, brought forth several articles, which he hastily crammed into the pockets. <br>“'''Barkers''' for me, Barney," said Toby Crackit. <br>“Here they are,” replied Barney, producing a pair of pistols.
#* {{quote-book|en|author=George MacDonald Fraser|title=[http://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flashman_(novel) Flashman]|year=1969|page=45|passage=Parkin, the Oxford Street gunmaker, sent me a brace of '''barkers''' in silver mountings, with my initials engraved—good for trade, I imagine.}}
# The spotted [[redshank]].

